ZwvZT_607eKu2tqpftbNAlx2HCgLa-s6B0jN2tfmaMofPaQd1DDBxQ20WXcW_WcygyH8vV-UJ8W8-GWf4xX7BlB5GrFRDEOecNEj2GdiQdCD9-21pwwmqcJ51jP7wsbq","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Considering form handling and navigation**\n\nI'm exploring options for a time budget of around 8k tokens, considering the remaining amount seems enough. I think it might be beneficial to fetch completions in an asynchronous way without initiating navigation until a timeout of 100ms. However, I might face challenges if the implementation isn't stable. Adding a 100ms delay before event submission could help and a debounce function might capture the form state better. I want to ensure that the user experience remains smooth and coherent without racing delays."},{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Evaluating timing and checkbox behavior**\n\nI'm considering whether to avoid timing hacks. Immediate navigation on an onchange event could disrupt interaction with native checkboxes, so it may be better to defer actions until after the user takes their action. A 150ms delay seems reasonable. I could create a helper script with a WeakMap to manage checkbox states effectively, especially for rapid toggles. I’ll also include an inline function for submitting the form while adhering to code conventions without relying on a specific framework. I want to ensure everything aligns correctly with testing expectations."}]},"output_index":0,"sequence_number":203}

